    "letter": "b",
    "value": "2"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1983-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(a=\\log_{60}3\\) and \\(b=\\log_{60}5,\\) \\[ \\begin{aligned} 1-a-b &=\\log_{60}\\frac{60}{15}=\\log_{60}4,\\\\ 1-b &=\\log_{60}\\frac{60}{5}=\\log_{60}12. \\end{aligned} \\] Therefore the exponent is \\(\\frac12\\log_{12}4,\\) and \\[ 12^{(\\frac{1}{2})\\log_{12}4}=\\sqrt4=2. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Express \\(1-a-b\\) and \\(1-b\\) as base-\\(60\\) logarithms",
        "Use \\(1-a-b=\\log_{60}4\\) and \\(1-b=\\log_{60}12\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
